        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "radiant_warmer_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": "Common OSCE questions and model answers",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "radiant_warmer_group_32",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is a radiant warmer?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A neonatal device that provides radiant heat to maintain the newborn's body temperature while allowing unrestricted access for examination and procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. What is its main advantage over an incubator?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It provides easier access to the newborn during resuscitation and procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. What is the normal target temperature for a newborn?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Generally 36.5–37.5°C."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. What is servo-control mode?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A mode in which the warmer adjusts heat output in response to feedback from a skin-temperature probe."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Why is the temperature probe important?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It provides the temperature feedback used by the control system to regulate heat output in servo mode."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. What can happen if the probe becomes detached?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The displayed temperature may no longer represent the infant's skin temperature accurately, potentially causing inappropriate heat delivery."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. Why are preterm infants more vulnerable to hypothermia?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "They have a larger surface-area-to-body-mass ratio, thinner skin, limited insulating fat, and immature thermoregulation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. What are the complications of radiant warming?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Hyperthermia, hypothermia if warming is inadequate, thermal injury, and increased insensible water loss."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q9. Why might an incubator be preferred for prolonged care?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An incubator provides an enclosed, controlled microenvironment that can reduce exposure to drafts and help manage humidity and temperature when indicated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q10. What would you do if a newborn remained hypothermic under a warmer?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "I would confirm the temperature, inspect the probe and device settings, assess the infant for underlying illness and other causes of heat loss, and escalate treatment according to the neonatal protocol."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "radiant_warmer_subsection_14",
          "subsection_title": "Common mistakes and examiner tips",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "radiant_warmer_group_33",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Confusing skin temperature with heater temperature"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The target refers to the infant's temperature, not the temperature of the heating element."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Incorrect probe placement"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An improperly secured probe can produce misleading readings and inappropriate heat delivery."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Ignoring the infant while watching the display"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Always assess the newborn directly. The display alone cannot identify every clinical problem."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "Failing to protect very preterm infants"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Use appropriate thermal-protection measures rather than relying on radiant heat alone."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Examiner tip: During the demonstration, identify the heating element, control panel, temperature probe, and mattress. Then explain servo-control mode, state the normal neonatal temperature range, and mention the risks of both hypothermia and hyperthermia."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "radiant_warmer_subsection_15",
          "subsection_title": "Mini-OSCE practice station",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "radiant_warmer_group_34",
              "group_title": "",
